## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design end-to-end computer vision systems that fuse perception with physics for deformable objects in cluttered environments, while also demonstrating expertise in efficient on-device adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- On-device few-shot adaptation
- 2.5D depth and surface normals representation
- Differentiable physics for stiffness estimation
- Grasp affordance learning with temporal consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: training loop for temporally-consistent affordance learning
for (batch of data) {
  const pred = model.forward(images);
  const affordanceLoss = computeBCE(pred.heatmap, target.heatmap);
  const depthLoss = computeL1(pred.depth, target.depth);
  const physicsLoss = computePhysicsConsistency(pred.stiffness, pred.depth);

  const totalLoss = affordanceLoss + depthLoss + physicsLoss;
  optimizer.step(totalLoss);
}

